# Install: copy this file to /etc/systemd/system/lm-verify-renovate.service
# (a real copy, NOT a symlink into this repo checkout - see foundry-playwright's
# ops/vm/foundry-verify.service for why: this unit controls User=/ExecStart=
# for what runs on the VM, and must only change via a deliberate manual step).
# ExecStart below points at a root-owned copy of verify-renovate-prs.sh, NOT
# at the copy inside FV_DIR - see the ExecStart comment for why, and re-copy
# it there (never symlink) after any change to the script, same as this
# file itself.
# Then: systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl enable --now lm-verify-renovate.timer
#
# --- Two identities, two checkouts, root as the only thing that touches both ---
# `foundry-verify` is the same credentialed system user as foundry-playwright's
# own nightly job - it has a repo-scoped `gh` token and an SSH commit-signing
# key in its $HOME, and owns FV_DIR (/opt/thefehrs-learning-manager), its own
# private checkout. verify-renovate-prs.sh only ever runs `git
# fetch`/`push`/`gh pr ...` there - plain network operations, never
# candidate-branch code.
#
# `lm-verify-runner` is a second, unprivileged system user created
# specifically for this job. It runs `git checkout`, `npm ci`, the build, and
# the actual Docker/Podman e2e suite - i.e. everything that executes code
# from a Renovate PR's dependency bump - in its own private workdir under its
# own $HOME. It has no gh token, no SSH key, and no filesystem access to
# FV_DIR or foundry-verify's $HOME at all, so a compromised dependency's
# install/postinstall script (CWE-829) has nothing to steal that could push,
# merge, or forge commits as foundry-verify.
#
# This unit runs as root (Type=oneshot, no User=) specifically so
# verify-renovate-prs.sh can dispatch every actual operation to the correct
# identity via `runuser -u <identity>`, which itself requires root - it does
# not authenticate like `su`, so a non-root caller can't use it at all. Root
# itself never touches git, gh, or npm directly, and never executes anything
# from a candidate branch: it only copies/chowns small `git bundle` files
# between FV_DIR and lm-verify-runner's workdir (see verify-renovate-prs.sh
# for why a bundle, not a shared checkout, is what moves between them - a
# shared .git would let the untrusted phase plant a hook that later executes
# as foundry-verify).
#
# One-time setup:
#   sudo useradd --system --create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin lm-verify-runner
#   # Non-overlapping range from foundry-verify's own 200000-265535 (see
#   # foundry-verify.service) - two rootless-Podman users sharing a subuid
#   # range would let one forge UIDs inside the other's user namespace.
#   sudo usermod --add-subuids 300000-365535 --add-subgids 300000-365535 lm-verify-runner
#   sudo loginctl enable-linger lm-verify-runner
#   sudo -u lm-verify-runner git config --global user.name "lm-verify-runner"
#   sudo -u lm-verify-runner git config --global user.email "lm-verify-runner@localhost"
#   # (no signing key for this identity - main has no signature requirement,
#   # unlike foundry-playwright's repo, so there's nothing to sign; and this
#   # identity's commits never reach GitHub directly anyway - foundry-verify
#   # re-commits nothing, it fast-forward-merges the runner's own commit in
#   # from a bundle, so no signing identity is needed here at all)
#
#   # FV_DIR: foundry-verify's own private checkout. lm-verify-runner gets
#   # NO standing access to this directory, or to foundry-playwright's .env -
#   # not even read. verify-renovate-prs.sh stages the Foundry credentials as
#   # a disposable per-run copy (root reads foundry-playwright's .env - it
#   # can read anything - and writes a fresh, shredded-after-use copy into
#   # lm-verify-runner's own workdir), rather than granting any persistent
#   # ACL: a compromised dependency's install/postinstall script would
#   # otherwise have a standing read grant on real Foundry credentials for
#   # the entire time it runs, well before the step that actually needs them.
#   sudo mkdir -p /opt/thefehrs-learning-manager
#   sudo chown foundry-verify:foundry-verify /opt/thefehrs-learning-manager
#   sudo chmod 700 /opt/thefehrs-learning-manager
#   sudo -u foundry-verify git clone https://github.com/TheFehr/thefehrs-learning-manager.git /opt/thefehrs-learning-manager
#
#   # Root-owned copy of the script this unit actually executes (see
#   # ExecStart below for why it can't be the copy inside FV_DIR).
#   sudo mkdir -p /opt/lm-verify-renovate
#   sudo cp /opt/thefehrs-learning-manager/ops/vm/verify-renovate-prs.sh /opt/lm-verify-renovate/
#   sudo chown -R root:root /opt/lm-verify-renovate
#   sudo chmod 755 /opt/lm-verify-renovate/verify-renovate-prs.sh
#
# No docker-group membership for lm-verify-runner, same reasoning as
# foundry-verify.service: this job fetches and executes third-party
# FoundryVTT/module/dependency content on every run, and docker-group access
# is root-equivalent. Containers run rootless via the same podman-docker
# wrapper already set up for foundry-verify - lm-verify-runner just needs
# its own subuid/subgid range (above), not a separate package install.

[Unit]
Description=Verify e2e for open thefehrs-learning-manager Renovate PRs
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/opt
# Deliberately NOT /opt/thefehrs-learning-manager/ops/vm/verify-renovate-prs.sh:
# that path is inside FV_DIR, which foundry-verify owns. This unit runs as
# root, so executing a script from a path a lower-privileged identity can
# write to would let a compromised foundry-verify replace it and gain root
# on the next timer fire - same reasoning as copying the unit files
# themselves rather than symlinking into the checkout (see top of this
# file), just applied to the script too.
ExecStart=/opt/lm-verify-renovate/verify-renovate-prs.sh
# The script stops after its first successful merge (see its comments - a
# merge rebases every other open PR, invalidating anything else verified
# this run) and caps failed attempts at MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_RUN=3, so worst
# case is 3 failed ~30-35min verify runs in a row. Sized with real margin
# over that, not for an open-ended hang - a run still going after 3h is
# stuck, not just slow.
TimeoutStartSec=3h
# Rootless Podman's conmon deliberately survives its parent dying, so a
# TimeoutStartSec kill (or any other abnormal exit) can leave a container
# running - which then holds verify-renovate-prs.sh's flock open via an
# inherited fd, silently blocking every future run until someone notices.
# The actual Foundry containers run under lm-verify-runner's namespace, not
# foundry-verify's or root's; force-remove anything it left behind, every
# time the service stops, regardless of why.
ExecStopPost=/bin/sh -c 'runuser -u lm-verify-runner -- podman ps -aq --filter "name=foundry-playwright-" | xargs -r runuser -u lm-verify-runner -- podman rm -f'
